      "body": "## Motivation\n\n#40857 lets EAGLE / EAGLE3 run with `--disaggregation-decode-enable-radix-cache`, so the decode tree of a non-Mamba model uses bigram keys: N cached positions are keyed by N + 1 token ids. Decode HiCache counts its prefix lengths (`l1`, `l2`, `l3`, `decode_prefix_len`) in bigrams, but passes them back as token counts in two places:\n\n- `_try_hicache_queue_load_back` rematches with `max_prefix_len=decode_prefix_len`. That becomes `RadixKey.limit` (a token cap), so the bigram key has `decode_prefix_len - 1` entries and the page-aligned rematch stops one page short. `device_prefix_len + loaded_len < decode_prefix_len` then always holds, the restore is marked FAILED, and every request that hits L2 or L3 is aborted (\"HiCache restore failed\").\n- `_start_hicache_prefetch` slices `l3` token ids for the prefetch, which `prefetch_from_storage` turns into `l3 - 1` bigrams, so the prefetch also lands one page short.\n\nMamba trees disable bigram keys and are not affected. The non-PD path passes every remaining token and is not affected either.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Both call sites add the bigram boundary token (`int(tree_core.is_eagle)`) when they turn a prefix length into a token count.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `test_decode_restore_rematch_covers_bigram_prefix` (CUDA): a real EAGLE `UnifiedRadixCache` with a host-only 16-position prefix, the real `match_kv_cache`, and the real `_try_hicache_queue_load_back`. It runs on both the Rust and the Python tree core.\n- `test_storage_probe_and_prefetch_use_node_handles` now also checks the EAGLE prefetch span.\n- Negative control: with the fix reverted, both tests fail. The real-cache test logs `HiCache load_back failed ... new_indices=12, expected decode_prefix_len=16`.\n- `test_decode_hicache_tree_core.py`, `test_decode_queue_cleanup.py`, `test_decode_radix_lock_ref.py` and `test_unified_radix_cache_unittest.py` all pass on 1x H200: 1386 passed, 1585 skipped, 89 subtests passed. The new class also passes with `SGLANG_UNIFIED_RADIX_TREE_CORE_BACKEND=python`.\n\n### Service-level check (8x B300, 1P1D over Mooncake)\n\nQwen3-8B, plus `Tengyunw/qwen3_8b_eagle3` in the EAGLE3 arms. The decode server runs `--disaggregation-decode-enable-radix-cache --enable-hierarchical-cache --hicache-write-policy write_through --max-total-tokens 6144`. Each run sends a 1600-token prompt twice, then 8 distinct 1600-token prompts so the first prompt's prefix is evicted to host, then the first prompt again with 4 more tokens.\n\n| tree | spec | last request | `load_back_tokens_total` delta | \"HiCache load_back failed\" log lines |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| main | none | 200 | 1600 | 0 |\n| main | EAGLE3 | **500** (decode_internal_error) | **0** | **5** (`new_indices=1472, expected decode_prefix_len=1536`) |\n| this PR | EAGLE3 | 200 | 1536 | 0 |\n| this PR | none | 200 | 1600 | 0 |\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39259695264](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39259695264)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39259695058](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39259695058)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39259695427](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39259695427)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
